\frametitle{Contributing}
\protect\phantomsection\label{contributing}
The CIF codebases are open for extension. Useful starting points:

\begin{itemize}
\tightlist
\item
  \textbf{Code and discussion}:
  \href{https://github.com/docxology/cognitive_integrity}{docxology/cognitive\_integrity
  on GitHub} (repository \texttt{discussions} for design questions).
\item
  \textbf{Adapters}: The Part\textasciitilde2 maturity scale has five
  levels; moving adapters from Level 3 to Level\textasciitilde4--5
  (Adaptive/Verified) is a high-leverage way to close the
  empirical--parametric gap. Ports to additional frameworks (e.g.,
  Semantic Kernel, Microsoft AutoGen) are welcome.
\item
  \textbf{Corpus}: The 950-attack set covers four categories; new
  instances for emergent misalignment and orchestrator compromise,
  following the Part\textasciitilde2 stratification, strengthen
  evaluation.
\item
  \textbf{Theory / verification}: FEP- and information-geometry--based
  monitoring (Direction 5--6) and extensions of the NuSMV/TLA+ specs
  (Part\textasciitilde2, Supplementary S04) to consensus and provenance
  are open. Formal proofs and measured evaluations belong in the same
  repository and review process as code.
\end{itemize}
